WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:06.030
<i>Everyone is searching for a new world</i>

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:12.140
<i>to attain that overflowing dream.</i>

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:17.710
<i>They all jump over the horizon,</i>

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:26.480
<i>regardless of what lies beyond.</i>

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:34.230
<i>We've run,</i>

00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:36.700
<i>we've dived into hope,</i>

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:39.570
<i>and forgotten only courage.</i>

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:44.310
<i>And we've been swept away by the crowd</i>

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:48.970
<i>only to lose something dear to us.</i>

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:54.650
<i>I smile with a twisted face,</i>

00:00:54.650 --> 00:01:01.320
<i>and it was the best smile I could put on.</i>

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:04.690
<i>The inside of my mask overflowed with tears</i>

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:12.330
<i>so I covered my wet mask
with yet another mask.</i>

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:17.240
<i>I continue to walk through
the flat battleground,</i>

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:22.480
<i>and I struggle, unable to warp.</i>

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:32.590
<i>The dream waits quietly on a cape far away.</i>

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:37.330
<i>Even if I fumble around clumsily,</i>

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:42.060
<i>I'm sure I'll still be
able to make it there.</i>

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:46.760
"Madoka's Birthday"

00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:48.090
<i>"Madoka's Birthday"
Sayoko-san was all smiles!</i>

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:49.360
<i>Sayoko-san was all smiles!</i>

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:52.060
That's great! She seems so happy!

00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:58.170
Just tell me what you know!
Stop hiding things from me!

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:01.340
<i>Terrible news, Narumi-san!</i>

00:02:01.340 --> 00:02:03.710
<i>Sayoko-san has disappeared!</i>

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:05.980
<i>Sayoko Shiranagatani, I take it?</i>

00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:07.850
<i>If you want things to stay peaceful</i>

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:11.650
<i>then you'll come to the fountain
in Central Park at 4:00.</i>

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:16.790
<i>What exactly am I doing?</i>

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:22.390
I've not much time left...

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:27.700
Sayoko is my only
remaining reason to live.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:34.970
She once said that her current
life was her entire life,

00:02:34.970 --> 00:02:38.080
that regardless of what
is hidden in her past,

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:43.240
believing in her happiness
now is everything to her...

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:45.990
This is how I think:

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:50.820
Even if Sayoko is a
Blade Child or whatnot,

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:54.630
as long as she is my salvation,

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:58.700
I wish to protect her, even
at the cost of my life.

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:04.700
And if she, herself, feels
happy about her current life...

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:10.280
...then she is not a cursed child at all.

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:15.270
"Mirror of the Heart"

00:03:22.790 --> 00:03:26.460
That's a bomb she's holding.

00:03:26.460 --> 00:03:29.360
If you can disarm it, you win.

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:31.930
If you can't, then the girl dies.

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:33.870
It's a simple enough game.

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:36.160
Take a look at the
shrubbery behind you.

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:43.580
It's a present.

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:46.150
I don't care if you and
your friend work together.

00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:49.050
I never said you had to
come alone, after all.

00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:51.720
But the instant you get near her...

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:53.950
Boom! The game's over.

00:03:53.950 --> 00:03:57.120
Well, good luck.

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:09.230
It's over if we get close to her, huh?

00:04:09.940 --> 00:04:11.940
<i>This doesn't look good...</i>

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:15.480
<i>Not only are the schematics
too difficult to decipher,</i>

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:17.880
<i>but I can't even get near her...</i>

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:34.260
<i>The person who set this up is nearby!</i>

00:04:44.140 --> 00:04:46.070
-Did you get it?
-Yes...

00:04:46.770 --> 00:04:50.100
Then it's time for a little walk.

00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:00.120
This is none of your business.

00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:02.410
I can do whatever I want.

00:06:29.670 --> 00:06:33.700
-Watch it!
-Sorry!

00:06:44.490 --> 00:06:47.260
It appears you haven't been followed.

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:50.190
In other words, there's one
of him and two of us,

00:06:50.190 --> 00:06:52.320
we should use that to our advantage.

00:06:58.130 --> 00:07:00.100
Have you figured out
the number of players?

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:03.310
There's one of me and two of you...

00:07:03.310 --> 00:07:06.880
It's up to you if the game
gets more exciting or not.

00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:10.000
I look forward to it. Give me some fun.

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:23.850
He seemed to hang up before
the ambulance passed by.

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:27.150
Which means...

00:07:29.430 --> 00:07:31.920
...the Hunter is within
two blocks of here.

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:37.600
If we're up against one
person, then we have a chance!

00:07:51.290 --> 00:07:55.460
The Hunter didn't give
a time limit. Right?

00:07:55.460 --> 00:07:58.660
That means the explosion
isn't triggered by a timer,

00:07:58.660 --> 00:08:01.060
but by remote control instead.

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:03.470
Even if we can't disarm the bomb,

00:08:03.470 --> 00:08:06.400
we can save her by catching the Hunter.

00:08:06.870 --> 00:08:09.300
We just don't let him use the detonator.

00:08:09.970 --> 00:08:12.540
Of course, it's up to you
if you want to go along

00:08:12.540 --> 00:08:14.740
with my plan or not.

00:08:14.740 --> 00:08:18.740
You do what you want.
I'll do what I want.

00:08:28.560 --> 00:08:29.960
Yo.

00:08:29.960 --> 00:08:32.630
How far are you going to make me walk?

00:08:32.630 --> 00:08:35.600
Hey now, don't sound so scared.

00:08:36.900 --> 00:08:39.230
Things are just about to get interesting.

00:08:39.230 --> 00:08:40.670
You're really going to enjoy this.

00:08:40.670 --> 00:08:42.070
A lot...

00:08:42.070 --> 00:08:45.640
What do you mean? What's going to happen?

00:08:45.640 --> 00:08:48.440
What are you planning to do with
my grandfather and the others?

00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:50.710
Nothing, really.

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:53.050
The tragedy has long since started.

00:08:53.050 --> 00:08:57.490
From the moment you were born
as a disgusting Blade Child...

00:08:57.490 --> 00:09:00.090
I don't know what you mean.

00:09:00.090 --> 00:09:02.080
You'll know soon enough.

00:09:34.360 --> 00:09:36.690
That's it, keep on walking...

00:09:36.690 --> 00:09:39.390
Despair is all that awaits you...

00:09:54.010 --> 00:09:56.750
<i>He wasn't more than two blocks back...</i>

00:09:56.750 --> 00:09:58.870
<i>The Hunter's somewhere here...</i>

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:03.050
Hello?

00:10:03.050 --> 00:10:06.820
Well? Can you see me, Little Narumi?

00:10:11.660 --> 00:10:13.390
<i>What's that sound?</i>

00:10:52.270 --> 00:10:54.740
<i>Where is he?!</i>

00:10:54.740 --> 00:10:58.430
Say, want me to tell you
what you're thinking?

00:10:58.640 --> 00:11:03.180
First you hide yourself, and
then Rutherford does too.

00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:05.510
Your opponent gets flustered
because he can't afford

00:11:05.510 --> 00:11:08.020
to lose sight of him too,
so he goes after him.

00:11:08.020 --> 00:11:10.450
You're planning to draw me out

00:11:10.450 --> 00:11:13.420
instead of disarming the bomb.

00:11:13.420 --> 00:11:15.920
Your strategy is to
catch me and prevent me

00:11:15.920 --> 00:11:17.860
from using the detonator.

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:20.700
Well? Did I guess right?

00:11:20.700 --> 00:11:22.360
<i>What is that sound?</i>

00:11:24.270 --> 00:11:27.340
I'm actually a nice guy, you know.

00:11:27.340 --> 00:11:29.570
Wouldn't you agree?

00:11:29.870 --> 00:11:35.210
I've given you bomb schematics
and hints like this.

00:11:35.210 --> 00:11:39.200
Even so, you can't catch me.

00:12:17.120 --> 00:12:19.320
<i>The Hunter would've
calculated from the beginning</i>

00:12:19.320 --> 00:12:21.990
<i>that Rutherford would
probably put himself at risk</i>

00:12:21.990 --> 00:12:24.060
<i>to save her.</i>

00:12:24.060 --> 00:12:26.560
<i>The Hunter's goal is
probably to toy with him</i>

00:12:26.560 --> 00:12:28.830
<i>before taking his life.</i>

00:12:28.830 --> 00:12:32.890
<i>But he hadn't counted
on me being involved...</i>

00:13:01.900 --> 00:13:04.570
The tragedy has long since started.

00:13:04.570 --> 00:13:09.060
From the moment you were born
as a disgusting Blade Child...

00:13:23.990 --> 00:13:25.650
Sorry!

00:13:36.160 --> 00:13:39.230
Man, I'm dying of boredom here.

00:13:39.230 --> 00:13:41.770
Do something, will ya?

00:13:41.770 --> 00:13:44.710
What's the matter? You're not responding.

00:13:46.340 --> 00:13:49.980
I just turned the timer on.

00:13:49.980 --> 00:13:51.750
You're tired of this too, aren't you?

00:13:51.750 --> 00:13:54.580
Let's put an end to this in five minutes.

00:14:04.230 --> 00:14:06.190
It's a marionette clock.

00:14:06.190 --> 00:14:08.700
That's definitely what that sound is.

00:14:08.700 --> 00:14:10.320
A marionette clock?

00:14:30.720 --> 00:14:31.510
This way!

00:14:33.760 --> 00:14:35.460
<i>Five minutes left!</i>

00:14:35.460 --> 00:14:37.080
<i>I've dug my own grave...</i>

00:14:46.970 --> 00:14:48.160
That's it!

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:52.340
<i>Now that he's set the timer</i>

00:14:52.340 --> 00:14:55.010
<i>I can get as close to her as I want.</i>

00:14:55.010 --> 00:14:57.050
<i>The fact that he handed
over the schematics</i>

00:14:57.050 --> 00:15:00.010
<i>shows that he's confident
it won't be dismantled.</i>

00:15:00.010 --> 00:15:03.010
<i>His overconfidence will be his undoing!</i>

00:15:06.790 --> 00:15:09.460
<i>The Hunter chose this street as the stage</i>

00:15:09.460 --> 00:15:11.630
<i>because of the way it feels.</i>

00:15:11.630 --> 00:15:14.730
<i>He normally walks around
this area for fun.</i>

00:15:14.730 --> 00:15:17.100
<i>He's probably somewhere in his twenties,</i>

00:15:17.100 --> 00:15:19.230
<i>and from his assertive actions</i>

00:15:19.230 --> 00:15:22.240
<i>there's no question he's
really confident about himself.</i>

00:15:22.240 --> 00:15:25.470
<i>He's convinced that he's
mentally and physically</i>

00:15:25.470 --> 00:15:28.870
<i>a perfect man with not
a shred of a complex...</i>

00:15:29.640 --> 00:15:32.940
<i>Naturally, he would have a
well-prepared escape plan!</i>

00:15:39.250 --> 00:15:42.190
<i>Your strategy is to
catch me and prevent me</i>

00:15:42.190 --> 00:15:43.590
<i>from using the detonator.</i>

00:15:43.590 --> 00:15:44.930
<i>Well? Did I guess right?</i>

00:15:44.930 --> 00:15:45.550
<i>Well? Did I guess right?</i>

00:15:51.130 --> 00:15:52.260
That's him!

00:15:54.770 --> 00:15:56.500
This is a bomb.

00:16:30.270 --> 00:16:31.970
Stop!

00:16:37.010 --> 00:16:38.410
Damn kid!

00:16:51.260 --> 00:16:53.230
The game is over.

00:17:00.270 --> 00:17:02.740
Damn! The disarm switch!

00:17:22.490 --> 00:17:24.460
Did you look inside the package?

00:17:24.460 --> 00:17:25.830
Who is this?

00:17:25.830 --> 00:17:28.420
I believe your future was inside it.

00:17:32.170 --> 00:17:35.470
There was nothing except the empty case.

00:17:35.470 --> 00:17:38.670
Yes. That is your future.

00:17:38.670 --> 00:17:41.040
Who am I speaking to?

00:17:41.040 --> 00:17:43.580
The Blade Children have no future.

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:46.450
No hope, no despair, nothing.

00:17:46.510 --> 00:17:49.580
There is nothing for the
Blade Children but ruin.

00:17:49.580 --> 00:17:53.190
I am Sayoko Shiranagatani.

00:17:53.190 --> 00:17:56.790
Even if a cursed fate does await me,

00:17:56.790 --> 00:17:59.360
I believe in now.

00:17:59.360 --> 00:18:02.190
I will believe in now and walk forward!

00:18:21.320 --> 00:18:24.420
A third party...

00:18:24.420 --> 00:18:28.390
I really doubt that
Hunter was joking around.

00:18:28.390 --> 00:18:31.650
There's no question that
a bomb was inside...

00:18:32.890 --> 00:18:37.300
Who would've switched the bomb, and why?

00:18:42.100 --> 00:18:46.200
<i>Eyes Rutherford was able
to disarm the bomb...</i>

00:18:47.180 --> 00:18:51.130
<i>I guess he didn't need me after all...</i>

00:18:51.910 --> 00:18:55.520
<i>I probably could have
dealt with this by myself.</i>

00:18:55.520 --> 00:19:00.980
<i>So why didn't I refuse
Little Narumi's help?</i>

00:19:11.730 --> 00:19:13.870
Where have you been?

00:19:13.870 --> 00:19:17.540
Oh, I was just asked to
do some unimportant work.

00:19:17.540 --> 00:19:19.010
It wasn't anything big.

00:19:19.010 --> 00:19:20.110
What kind of work?

00:19:20.110 --> 00:19:24.080
It was like a missing-children's search.

00:19:24.080 --> 00:19:26.980
The police headquarters gets
missing-children's search requests?

00:19:26.980 --> 00:19:29.450
Apparently it has, recently.

00:19:29.450 --> 00:19:31.420
<i>The economy is bad...</i>

00:19:31.420 --> 00:19:33.190
Yes, that might be it...

00:19:33.190 --> 00:19:37.530
I wish they would consider the
headquarters' dignity for once...

00:19:37.530 --> 00:19:39.590
Well, the world is peaceful...

00:19:39.590 --> 00:19:41.160
I wonder sometimes...

00:19:41.160 --> 00:19:43.560
Even so, it's better than
being deprived of work.

00:19:43.560 --> 00:19:46.230
Eh? You want to look for missing kids?

00:19:46.230 --> 00:19:48.840
Sure. I'll do anything.

00:19:48.840 --> 00:19:50.570
An assistant inspector for the
metropolitan police department,

00:19:50.570 --> 00:19:52.010
searching for lost kids?

00:19:52.010 --> 00:19:54.410
I suppose that's not uncommon either.

00:19:54.410 --> 00:19:56.010
<i>The economy is bad...</i>

00:19:56.010 --> 00:19:59.210
...which is just a stupid excuse!

00:20:02.480 --> 00:20:05.520
-Well, let's enjoy some drinks.
-All right.

00:20:05.520 --> 00:20:08.290
Go ahead and order whatever you'd like.

00:20:08.290 --> 00:20:12.430
Thank you. But we always
wind up splitting the cost.

00:20:12.430 --> 00:20:13.430
Yeah, well...

00:20:13.430 --> 00:20:16.530
Incidentally, how much spending
money do you get a month?

00:20:16.530 --> 00:20:19.730
-About 30,000 yen.
-Wow, that must be pretty tough...

00:20:19.730 --> 00:20:22.300
I have a car loan and such...

00:20:22.300 --> 00:20:25.970
It's all over if you spend your
life just to pay off loans.

00:20:25.970 --> 00:20:27.410
Do you think?

00:20:27.410 --> 00:20:29.410
You'll never find your purpose in life

00:20:29.410 --> 00:20:31.280
as long as you're buried
under possessions.

00:20:31.280 --> 00:20:32.450
That's food for thought.

00:20:32.450 --> 00:20:35.220
Excess things in your life are a waste.

00:20:35.220 --> 00:20:38.750
Walk straight toward your goal.

00:20:38.750 --> 00:20:42.220
Do that, and you'll start to see
true hope for the first time.

00:20:42.220 --> 00:20:43.090
I'm about to cry.

00:20:43.090 --> 00:20:45.560
But that's what I do and
now I'm deprived of my work...

00:20:45.560 --> 00:20:47.160
<i>The economy is bad...</i>

00:20:47.160 --> 00:20:49.360
Then stop taking out stupid loans!

00:20:49.360 --> 00:20:51.370
I can do whatever I want!

00:20:51.370 --> 00:20:54.070
I've been considering changing
professions lately...

00:20:54.070 --> 00:20:56.040
Here you are, one vinegar cucumber!

00:21:05.850 --> 00:21:11.550
<i>A sweet scent washes into my throat</i>

00:21:11.550 --> 00:21:18.250
<i>and my feelings continuously overflow...</i>

00:21:30.370 --> 00:21:36.410
<i>Don't look at me with that same gaze</i>

00:21:36.410 --> 00:21:42.050
<i>that's like you're following a soccer ball.</i>

00:21:42.050 --> 00:21:47.960
<i>I've already grown used to
my third year at the office,</i>

00:21:47.960 --> 00:21:54.530
<i>but did I lose something instead?</i>

00:21:54.530 --> 00:22:00.270
<i>Those days long ago when we
would talk about anything...</i>

00:22:00.270 --> 00:22:05.470
<i>We're finally old enough now</i>

00:22:05.470 --> 00:22:11.310
<i>to have those slightly awkward
discussions about love.</i>

00:22:11.310 --> 00:22:22.920
<i>A single day seems so long,
but a whole year ends so quickly.</i>

00:22:22.920 --> 00:22:28.700
<i>A whole year seems so short,</i>

00:22:28.700 --> 00:22:35.000
<i>but how well will I be able
to live the rest of my life?</i>

00:22:38.870 --> 00:22:40.940
Time for Hiyono's Useful News Report!

00:22:40.940 --> 00:22:44.940
Flower petals flutter and
hearts go thump-thump!

00:22:44.940 --> 00:22:47.340
Next episode's highlight is telepathy!

00:22:47.340 --> 00:22:50.550
People can grow stronger when they
think of someone dear to them!

00:22:50.550 --> 00:22:52.620
Because no matter how
far apart they might be,

00:22:52.620 --> 00:22:57.620
a gentle wind will carry their
sorrow and love on flower petals!

00:22:57.620 --> 00:23:00.120
On the next Spiral: Bond of Reasoning...

00:23:00.120 --> 00:23:01.490
Whispering Shadows

00:23:01.490 --> 00:23:04.530
Red light! No crossing
the street all at once!

00:23:04.530 --> 00:23:06.690
That's all for today's
Hiyono's Playhouse!
